  ('ai:ai-batch-09:30441dfcb2fe','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','How does the memory palace technique work?',array['by repeating items aloud many times','by placing items in imagined locations along a route','by linking items to numbers','by writing items down in order']::text[],'B','''...mentally place the items you want to remember in specific locations along a route.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','The ''memory palace'' is a technique dating back to ancient Greece. To use it, you imagine a familiar building and mentally place the items you want to remember in specific locations along a route through it. Later, by walking through the building in your mind, you retrieve the items in order. Memory champions routinely use the method to memorise long sequences of numbers or cards. Researchers have found that ordinary people trained in the technique for several weeks show marked improvements in recall, and that these gains can persist for months.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:4c229aa513a4','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What did research find about ordinary people trained in the technique?',array['Their recall improved markedly and the gains lasted.','The technique only works for numbers.','They became memory champions.','They forgot more quickly.']::text[],'A','''...show marked improvements in recall, and... these gains can persist for months.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','The ''memory palace'' is a technique dating back to ancient Greece. To use it, you imagine a familiar building and mentally place the items you want to remember in specific locations along a route through it. Later, by walking through the building in your mind, you retrieve the items in order. Memory champions routinely use the method to memorise long sequences of numbers or cards. Researchers have found that ordinary people trained in the technique for several weeks show marked improvements in recall, and that these gains can persist for months.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:3f20d716bc12','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Where does the technique originate?',array['medieval monasteries','ancient Greece','modern psychology','memory competitions']::text[],'B','''...a technique dating back to ancient Greece.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','The ''memory palace'' is a technique dating back to ancient Greece. To use it, you imagine a familiar building and mentally place the items you want to remember in specific locations along a route through it. Later, by walking through the building in your mind, you retrieve the items in order. Memory champions routinely use the method to memorise long sequences of numbers or cards. Researchers have found that ordinary people trained in the technique for several weeks show marked improvements in recall, and that these gains can persist for months.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:cbd696be9daa','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','According to economic historians, what is a ''myth''?',array['that work is insecure today','that women worked in agriculture','that a job for life was once the norm','that migrants moved often']::text[],'C','''The notion that a ''job for life'' was once the norm is... something of a myth.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','The notion that a ''job for life'' was once the norm is, according to economic historians, something of a myth. While many workers in the mid-twentieth century did remain with a single employer for decades, large sections of the workforce — particularly women, migrants and those in agriculture — experienced insecure and seasonal work throughout. What has changed, they argue, is less the existence of precarious work than its spread into professions that were previously regarded as secure.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:80e49aad2ca6','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Which groups experienced insecure work in the mid-twentieth century?',array['factory managers','only professionals','women, migrants and agricultural workers','civil servants']::text[],'C','''...particularly women, migrants and those in agriculture.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','The notion that a ''job for life'' was once the norm is, according to economic historians, something of a myth. While many workers in the mid-twentieth century did remain with a single employer for decades, large sections of the workforce — particularly women, migrants and those in agriculture — experienced insecure and seasonal work throughout. What has changed, they argue, is less the existence of precarious work than its spread into professions that were previously regarded as secure.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:a3ac66b79c59','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What, according to historians, has changed?',array['Precarious work has spread into previously secure professions.','Everyone now has a job for life.','Precarious work has disappeared.','Agriculture has become secure.']::text[],'A','''...less the existence of precarious work than its spread into professions...''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','The notion that a ''job for life'' was once the norm is, according to economic historians, something of a myth. While many workers in the mid-twentieth century did remain with a single employer for decades, large sections of the workforce — particularly women, migrants and those in agriculture — experienced insecure and seasonal work throughout. What has changed, they argue, is less the existence of precarious work than its spread into professions that were previously regarded as secure.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:38b5c9c92ae3','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What causes the urban heat island effect?',array['industrial pollution only','too many people','dark surfaces and lack of vegetation','the shape of rivers']::text[],'C','''Dark surfaces... absorb heat... while the lack of vegetation reduces cooling.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Cities are typically several degrees warmer than the surrounding countryside, a phenomenon known as the urban heat island effect. Dark surfaces such as asphalt and roofs absorb heat during the day and release it at night, while the lack of vegetation reduces cooling through evaporation. As heatwaves become more frequent, planners are experimenting with reflective roofing materials, street trees and ''pocket parks''. Such measures can lower local temperatures significantly, though their effectiveness depends on being implemented at scale.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:1363827fa764','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What condition is attached to the effectiveness of cooling measures?',array['They only work in winter.','They must be cheap.','They must be implemented at scale.','They require new laws.']::text[],'C','''...their effectiveness depends on being implemented at scale.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Cities are typically several degrees warmer than the surrounding countryside, a phenomenon known as the urban heat island effect. Dark surfaces such as asphalt and roofs absorb heat during the day and release it at night, while the lack of vegetation reduces cooling through evaporation. As heatwaves become more frequent, planners are experimenting with reflective roofing materials, street trees and ''pocket parks''. Such measures can lower local temperatures significantly, though their effectiveness depends on being implemented at scale.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:df9b2f7709f7','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','When do dark surfaces release the heat they absorb?',array['only in summer','when it rains','in the morning','at night']::text[],'D','''...absorb heat during the day and release it at night.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Cities are typically several degrees warmer than the surrounding countryside, a phenomenon known as the urban heat island effect. Dark surfaces such as asphalt and roofs absorb heat during the day and release it at night, while the lack of vegetation reduces cooling through evaporation. As heatwaves become more frequent, planners are experimenting with reflective roofing materials, street trees and ''pocket parks''. Such measures can lower local temperatures significantly, though their effectiveness depends on being implemented at scale.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:457210ab8180','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What do we actually do when we think we are multitasking?',array['work slower on each task simultaneously','switch rapidly between tasks','use different brains','focus on one task only']::text[],'B','''...usually rapid switching between tasks.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Despite the widespread belief that multitasking boosts productivity, research consistently suggests otherwise. What we experience as doing several things at once is usually rapid switching between tasks, and each switch carries a cost in time and accuracy. Heavy multitaskers, studies indicate, are often worse at filtering out irrelevant information. Nevertheless, some combinations — such as listening to music while performing a routine physical task — appear to cause little interference, because they draw on different mental resources.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:5aca4f38dc99','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What do studies say about heavy multitaskers?',array['They are more productive.','They never make mistakes.','They have better memories.','They are worse at filtering out irrelevant information.']::text[],'D','''Heavy multitaskers... are often worse at filtering out irrelevant information.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Despite the widespread belief that multitasking boosts productivity, research consistently suggests otherwise. What we experience as doing several things at once is usually rapid switching between tasks, and each switch carries a cost in time and accuracy. Heavy multitaskers, studies indicate, are often worse at filtering out irrelevant information. Nevertheless, some combinations — such as listening to music while performing a routine physical task — appear to cause little interference, because they draw on different mental resources.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:348e38e1c799','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Why can some task combinations cause little interference?',array['They use different mental resources.','They involve music.','They are done at night.','They are both difficult.']::text[],'A','''...because they draw on different mental resources.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Despite the widespread belief that multitasking boosts productivity, research consistently suggests otherwise. What we experience as doing several things at once is usually rapid switching between tasks, and each switch carries a cost in time and accuracy. Heavy multitaskers, studies indicate, are often worse at filtering out irrelevant information. Nevertheless, some combinations — such as listening to music while performing a routine physical task — appear to cause little interference, because they draw on different mental resources.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:fff6459a451a','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What is remarkable about some placebo studies?',array['Placebos cured serious diseases.','Placebos worked even when patients knew they were inactive.','Placebos made patients worse.','Doctors could not tell them apart.']::text[],'B','''...placebos can work even when patients are told they are taking an inactive pill.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','The placebo effect — improvement in a patient''s condition after receiving a treatment with no active ingredient — is one of the most intriguing phenomena in medicine. Remarkably, some studies have found that placebos can work even when patients are told they are taking an inactive pill. Researchers believe that expectations and the ritual of treatment trigger real changes in the brain, particularly in the perception of pain. However, placebos have little effect on the underlying causes of serious diseases, which is why their use outside research raises ethical questions.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:09eabe2ae8f2','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What do researchers think triggers the placebo effect?',array['patients'' diets','the colour of pills','hidden active ingredients','expectations and the ritual of treatment']::text[],'D','''...expectations and the ritual of treatment trigger real changes in the brain.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','The placebo effect — improvement in a patient''s condition after receiving a treatment with no active ingredient — is one of the most intriguing phenomena in medicine. Remarkably, some studies have found that placebos can work even when patients are told they are taking an inactive pill. Researchers believe that expectations and the ritual of treatment trigger real changes in the brain, particularly in the perception of pain. However, placebos have little effect on the underlying causes of serious diseases, which is why their use outside research raises ethical questions.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:811143da2803','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Why does using placebos outside research raise ethical questions?',array['Patients refuse them.','They don''t treat the underlying causes of serious disease.','They always cause side effects.','They are too expensive.']::text[],'B','''...placebos have little effect on the underlying causes of serious diseases.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','The placebo effect — improvement in a patient''s condition after receiving a treatment with no active ingredient — is one of the most intriguing phenomena in medicine. Remarkably, some studies have found that placebos can work even when patients are told they are taking an inactive pill. Researchers believe that expectations and the ritual of treatment trigger real changes in the brain, particularly in the perception of pain. However, placebos have little effect on the underlying causes of serious diseases, which is why their use outside research raises ethical questions.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:adc0a6ca554a','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','In which area are placebo effects particularly noted?',array['bone growth','blood type','the perception of pain','infections']::text[],'C','''...particularly in the perception of pain.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','The placebo effect — improvement in a patient''s condition after receiving a treatment with no active ingredient — is one of the most intriguing phenomena in medicine. Remarkably, some studies have found that placebos can work even when patients are told they are taking an inactive pill. Researchers believe that expectations and the ritual of treatment trigger real changes in the brain, particularly in the perception of pain. However, placebos have little effect on the underlying causes of serious diseases, which is why their use outside research raises ethical questions.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:05acfa9778f9','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What proportion of languages may disappear by the end of the century?',array['almost all','none','about a tenth','around half']::text[],'D','''...around half may disappear by the end of the century.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Of the roughly 7,000 languages spoken today, linguists estimate that around half may disappear by the end of the century. When a language dies, it is not only words that are lost but also knowledge about local plants, medicine and history encoded in it. Revitalisation efforts have had notable successes: Welsh, for instance, has seen a rise in speakers thanks to bilingual education and broadcasting. Yet such efforts depend heavily on the commitment of communities themselves; government policy alone is rarely sufficient.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:df306876dcaf','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What is lost when a language dies, according to the text?',array['nothing important','only grammar rules','mainly written texts','knowledge encoded in it, as well as words']::text[],'D','''...not only words that are lost but also knowledge about local plants, medicine and history.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Of the roughly 7,000 languages spoken today, linguists estimate that around half may disappear by the end of the century. When a language dies, it is not only words that are lost but also knowledge about local plants, medicine and history encoded in it. Revitalisation efforts have had notable successes: Welsh, for instance, has seen a rise in speakers thanks to bilingual education and broadcasting. Yet such efforts depend heavily on the commitment of communities themselves; government policy alone is rarely sufficient.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:8c0d223c314e','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What has helped Welsh?',array['online translation','bilingual education and broadcasting','tourism','banning English in Wales']::text[],'B','''...thanks to bilingual education and broadcasting.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Of the roughly 7,000 languages spoken today, linguists estimate that around half may disappear by the end of the century. When a language dies, it is not only words that are lost but also knowledge about local plants, medicine and history encoded in it. Revitalisation efforts have had notable successes: Welsh, for instance, has seen a rise in speakers thanks to bilingual education and broadcasting. Yet such efforts depend heavily on the commitment of communities themselves; government policy alone is rarely sufficient.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:54be3e46f38b','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What does language revitalisation depend on most?',array['government policy alone','community commitment','foreign funding','dictionaries']::text[],'B','''...depend heavily on the commitment of communities themselves.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Of the roughly 7,000 languages spoken today, linguists estimate that around half may disappear by the end of the century. When a language dies, it is not only words that are lost but also knowledge about local plants, medicine and history encoded in it. Revitalisation efforts have had notable successes: Welsh, for instance, has seen a rise in speakers thanks to bilingual education and broadcasting. Yet such efforts depend heavily on the commitment of communities themselves; government policy alone is rarely sufficient.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:d15e2e3d1312','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What do minimalism''s advocates claim?',array['Objects bring security.','Minimalism is expensive.','Decluttering reduces stress and frees resources for experiences.','Owning more makes people happier.']::text[],'C','''...decluttering reduces stress and frees up time and money for experiences.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Minimalism, the practice of deliberately owning fewer possessions, has attracted a devoted following. Its advocates claim that decluttering reduces stress and frees up time and money for experiences rather than objects. Sceptics, however, point out that minimalism is often marketed as a lifestyle product in itself, complete with expensive ''essential'' items and books. They also note that choosing to own little is a privilege available mainly to those who could afford to replace things if needed.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:5bc075bd0bf9','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What irony do sceptics point out?',array['Minimalists own more than others.','It increases stress.','Minimalism is free.','Minimalism is itself marketed with expensive products.']::text[],'D','''...minimalism is often marketed as a lifestyle product in itself.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Minimalism, the practice of deliberately owning fewer possessions, has attracted a devoted following. Its advocates claim that decluttering reduces stress and frees up time and money for experiences rather than objects. Sceptics, however, point out that minimalism is often marketed as a lifestyle product in itself, complete with expensive ''essential'' items and books. They also note that choosing to own little is a privilege available mainly to those who could afford to replace things if needed.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:27b3e5b47506','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Why do sceptics call minimalism a privilege?',array['It requires a large house.','It needs professional help.','Only rich countries allow it.','Only those who can afford to replace things can choose to own little.']::text[],'D','''...a privilege available mainly to those who could afford to replace things if needed.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Minimalism, the practice of deliberately owning fewer possessions, has attracted a devoted following. Its advocates claim that decluttering reduces stress and frees up time and money for experiences rather than objects. Sceptics, however, point out that minimalism is often marketed as a lifestyle product in itself, complete with expensive ''essential'' items and books. They also note that choosing to own little is a privilege available mainly to those who could afford to replace things if needed.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:8abe611bb424','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','How are crowdfunding backers different from investors?',array['They usually get a reward, not a share of profits.','They own the company.','They always get their money back.','They pay interest.']::text[],'A','''...they usually receive a reward rather than a share of profits.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Crowdfunding platforms allow creators to raise money directly from the public, bypassing banks and traditional investors. Many projects, from board games to documentaries, owe their existence to such campaigns. However, backers are not investors in the usual sense: they usually receive a reward rather than a share of profits, and there is no guarantee the product will ever be delivered. Consumer groups advise backers to research the creator''s track record and to treat contributions as support for an idea rather than a purchase.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:67895e8818eb','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What risk do backers face?',array['The product may never be delivered.','They must pay tax twice.','They lose their bank accounts.','They become liable for debts.']::text[],'A','''...there is no guarantee the product will ever be delivered.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Crowdfunding platforms allow creators to raise money directly from the public, bypassing banks and traditional investors. Many projects, from board games to documentaries, owe their existence to such campaigns. However, backers are not investors in the usual sense: they usually receive a reward rather than a share of profits, and there is no guarantee the product will ever be delivered. Consumer groups advise backers to research the creator''s track record and to treat contributions as support for an idea rather than a purchase.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:5c3addb49fd0','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What do consumer groups advise?',array['Research the creator and treat it as support, not a purchase.','Never use crowdfunding.','Back as many projects as possible.','Ask banks for advice.']::text[],'A','''...research the creator''s track record and... treat contributions as support for an idea rather than a purchase.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Crowdfunding platforms allow creators to raise money directly from the public, bypassing banks and traditional investors. Many projects, from board games to documentaries, owe their existence to such campaigns. However, backers are not investors in the usual sense: they usually receive a reward rather than a share of profits, and there is no guarantee the product will ever be delivered. Consumer groups advise backers to research the creator''s track record and to treat contributions as support for an idea rather than a purchase.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:3a947d2715a6','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What pattern of sleep does Ekirch describe?',array['two phases with a waking interval at night','one long sleep','short naps every few hours','sleeping only in the day']::text[],'A','''...slept in two phases: a ''first sleep''... followed by a period of wakefulness... and then a ''second sleep''.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Historian Roger Ekirch has argued that before the spread of artificial lighting, people in Western Europe commonly slept in two phases: a ''first sleep'' beginning soon after dusk, followed by a period of wakefulness in the middle of the night, and then a ''second sleep'' until morning. During the waking interval people prayed, read, talked or visited neighbours. Ekirch suggests that some modern cases of waking in the night may be a return to this older pattern rather than a disorder.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:48ba61bfd876','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What changed this sleep pattern, according to Ekirch?',array['new religious rules','industrial noise','changes in diet','the spread of artificial lighting']::text[],'D','''...before the spread of artificial lighting...''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Historian Roger Ekirch has argued that before the spread of artificial lighting, people in Western Europe commonly slept in two phases: a ''first sleep'' beginning soon after dusk, followed by a period of wakefulness in the middle of the night, and then a ''second sleep'' until morning. During the waking interval people prayed, read, talked or visited neighbours. Ekirch suggests that some modern cases of waking in the night may be a return to this older pattern rather than a disorder.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:80a4bcea9f8b','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What does Ekirch suggest about modern night waking?',array['It never happens.','It is caused by reading.','It may be a return to an older pattern.','It is always a disorder.']::text[],'C','''...may be a return to this older pattern rather than a disorder.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Historian Roger Ekirch has argued that before the spread of artificial lighting, people in Western Europe commonly slept in two phases: a ''first sleep'' beginning soon after dusk, followed by a period of wakefulness in the middle of the night, and then a ''second sleep'' until morning. During the waking interval people prayed, read, talked or visited neighbours. Ekirch suggests that some modern cases of waking in the night may be a return to this older pattern rather than a disorder.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:b05a83eab18b','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What did the study find after moving to open-plan offices?',array['Face-to-face interaction fell by about 70%.','Productivity rose by 70%.','Email use fell.','Face-to-face interaction doubled.']::text[],'A','''...face-to-face interaction fell by around 70%, while email and messaging increased.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Open-plan offices were widely adopted on the assumption that removing walls would encourage collaboration. A study conducted at two large companies, however, found that after moving to open-plan spaces, face-to-face interaction fell by around 70%, while email and messaging increased. The researchers suggested that employees, feeling observed and seeking privacy, withdrew into digital communication. The findings have prompted some firms to provide a mix of open areas and quiet rooms.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:43b045d9361b','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Why did employees withdraw into digital communication?',array['Managers told them to.','There were no meeting rooms.','They felt observed and wanted privacy.','They preferred typing.']::text[],'C','''...employees, feeling observed and seeking privacy, withdrew into digital communication.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Open-plan offices were widely adopted on the assumption that removing walls would encourage collaboration. A study conducted at two large companies, however, found that after moving to open-plan spaces, face-to-face interaction fell by around 70%, while email and messaging increased. The researchers suggested that employees, feeling observed and seeking privacy, withdrew into digital communication. The findings have prompted some firms to provide a mix of open areas and quiet rooms.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:e84017d256d0','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What have some firms done in response?',array['provided a mix of open areas and quiet rooms','returned to private offices for everyone','closed their offices','banned email']::text[],'A','''...provide a mix of open areas and quiet rooms.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Open-plan offices were widely adopted on the assumption that removing walls would encourage collaboration. A study conducted at two large companies, however, found that after moving to open-plan spaces, face-to-face interaction fell by around 70%, while email and messaging increased. The researchers suggested that employees, feeling observed and seeking privacy, withdrew into digital communication. The findings have prompted some firms to provide a mix of open areas and quiet rooms.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:be035a9d5af8','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Why does the text call the climate–migration relationship ''complex''?',array['Climate change has no effect on migration.','Only rich people migrate.','Environmental pressures interact with poverty and conflict.','Migration always crosses borders.']::text[],'C','''Environmental pressures... interact with poverty, conflict and political instability.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Climate change is increasingly cited as a driver of migration, yet the relationship is complex. Environmental pressures such as drought rarely act alone; they interact with poverty, conflict and political instability. Moreover, the poorest households often lack the resources to move at all, leaving them ''trapped'' in vulnerable areas. Most climate-related movement is expected to occur within countries rather than across borders, a point often overlooked in public debate.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:189e27d1bf64','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Why might the poorest households be ''trapped''?',array['They prefer to stay.','Borders are closed.','They lack resources to move.','They are protected by governments.']::text[],'C','''...the poorest households often lack the resources to move at all.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Climate change is increasingly cited as a driver of migration, yet the relationship is complex. Environmental pressures such as drought rarely act alone; they interact with poverty, conflict and political instability. Moreover, the poorest households often lack the resources to move at all, leaving them ''trapped'' in vulnerable areas. Most climate-related movement is expected to occur within countries rather than across borders, a point often overlooked in public debate.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:6bea4f1dfc58','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What point is often overlooked in public debate?',array['Droughts are rare.','Most migrants are wealthy.','Most climate-related movement is within countries.','Migration is decreasing.']::text[],'C','''Most climate-related movement is expected to occur within countries rather than across borders.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Climate change is increasingly cited as a driver of migration, yet the relationship is complex. Environmental pressures such as drought rarely act alone; they interact with poverty, conflict and political instability. Moreover, the poorest households often lack the resources to move at all, leaving them ''trapped'' in vulnerable areas. Most climate-related movement is expected to occur within countries rather than across borders, a point often overlooked in public debate.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:192f4647e717','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What is the purpose of traffic light labels?',array['to show the price','to help consumers choose healthier food quickly','to indicate cooking times','to show where food comes from']::text[],'B','''...intended to help consumers make healthier choices at a glance.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Front-of-pack labels using a ''traffic light'' system — red, amber and green for fat, sugar and salt — are intended to help consumers make healthier choices at a glance. Evidence suggests they do influence purchasing, particularly when shoppers are short of time. Manufacturers have also reformulated some products to avoid red labels. Critics, however, argue that the system can be misleading: a small portion of an unhealthy product may score better than a nutritious food eaten in a larger portion.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:076ae2ece81a','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','How have manufacturers responded?',array['by reformulating some products','by raising prices','by removing labels','by ignoring them']::text[],'A','''Manufacturers have also reformulated some products to avoid red labels.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Front-of-pack labels using a ''traffic light'' system — red, amber and green for fat, sugar and salt — are intended to help consumers make healthier choices at a glance. Evidence suggests they do influence purchasing, particularly when shoppers are short of time. Manufacturers have also reformulated some products to avoid red labels. Critics, however, argue that the system can be misleading: a small portion of an unhealthy product may score better than a nutritious food eaten in a larger portion.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:80a57f954bed','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What criticism is made of the system?',array['Portion sizes can make it misleading.','It ignores sugar.','It is only in English.','It uses too many colours.']::text[],'A','''...a small portion of an unhealthy product may score better than a nutritious food eaten in a larger portion.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Front-of-pack labels using a ''traffic light'' system — red, amber and green for fat, sugar and salt — are intended to help consumers make healthier choices at a glance. Evidence suggests they do influence purchasing, particularly when shoppers are short of time. Manufacturers have also reformulated some products to avoid red labels. Critics, however, argue that the system can be misleading: a small portion of an unhealthy product may score better than a nutritious food eaten in a larger portion.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:3a52b6182eea','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Why is digital material described as fragile?',array['Paper lasts longer than anything.','Formats become obsolete and media degrade.','Computers are expensive.','Digital files are too large.']::text[],'B','''File formats become obsolete, storage media degrade, and websites disappear.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Digital archives promise to preserve information indefinitely, yet digital material is in some respects more fragile than paper. File formats become obsolete, storage media degrade, and websites disappear without trace — a phenomenon sometimes called ''link rot''. Archivists warn of a potential ''digital dark age'' in which future historians may find records of the early twenty-first century harder to access than those of previous centuries. Initiatives such as web archiving aim to counter this, but they can capture only a fraction of what is published online.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:3592be53a87a','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What is ''link rot''?',array['viruses in archives','broken computer cables','slow internet','websites disappearing without trace']::text[],'D','''...websites disappear without trace — a phenomenon sometimes called ''link rot''.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Digital archives promise to preserve information indefinitely, yet digital material is in some respects more fragile than paper. File formats become obsolete, storage media degrade, and websites disappear without trace — a phenomenon sometimes called ''link rot''. Archivists warn of a potential ''digital dark age'' in which future historians may find records of the early twenty-first century harder to access than those of previous centuries. Initiatives such as web archiving aim to counter this, but they can capture only a fraction of what is published online.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:c63520038911','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What limitation of web archiving is mentioned?',array['It destroys original files.','It only stores images.','It is illegal.','It captures only a fraction of online content.']::text[],'D','''...they can capture only a fraction of what is published online.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Digital archives promise to preserve information indefinitely, yet digital material is in some respects more fragile than paper. File formats become obsolete, storage media degrade, and websites disappear without trace — a phenomenon sometimes called ''link rot''. Archivists warn of a potential ''digital dark age'' in which future historians may find records of the early twenty-first century harder to access than those of previous centuries. Initiatives such as web archiving aim to counter this, but they can capture only a fraction of what is published online.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:b282732caab6','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Which outlets often enjoy higher trust?',array['social media influencers','partisan websites','commercial tabloids','public service broadcasters']::text[],'D','''...public service broadcasters often enjoy higher levels of confidence.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Surveys indicate that trust in news media has declined in many countries, with audiences increasingly turning to social media for information. Yet trust varies considerably by outlet: public service broadcasters often enjoy higher levels of confidence than commercial or partisan sources. Some researchers argue that the decline reflects not only concerns about accuracy but also a sense that journalists are out of touch with ordinary people''s concerns.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:10ceaa00ab29','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What else, besides accuracy concerns, may explain declining trust?',array['the price of newspapers','longer articles','a sense that journalists are out of touch','fewer journalists']::text[],'C','''...a sense that journalists are out of touch with ordinary people''s concerns.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Surveys indicate that trust in news media has declined in many countries, with audiences increasingly turning to social media for information. Yet trust varies considerably by outlet: public service broadcasters often enjoy higher levels of confidence than commercial or partisan sources. Some researchers argue that the decline reflects not only concerns about accuracy but also a sense that journalists are out of touch with ordinary people''s concerns.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:0b29740d315e','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Where are audiences increasingly getting information?',array['printed newspapers','social media','libraries','radio only']::text[],'B','''...audiences increasingly turning to social media for information.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Surveys indicate that trust in news media has declined in many countries, with audiences increasingly turning to social media for information. Yet trust varies considerably by outlet: public service broadcasters often enjoy higher levels of confidence than commercial or partisan sources. Some researchers argue that the decline reflects not only concerns about accuracy but also a sense that journalists are out of touch with ordinary people''s concerns.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:cec6431a3678','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What is a ''fifteen-minute city''?',array['a city with 15-minute parking limits','a city where daily needs are within a short walk or cycle','a city that takes 15 minutes to cross by car','a city with fast trains']::text[],'B','''...residents can reach most daily needs... within a fifteen-minute walk or cycle.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','''Fifteen-minute cities'' are urban areas designed so that residents can reach most daily needs — shops, schools, health services and parks — within a fifteen-minute walk or cycle. Proponents argue the model reduces car dependence, improves health and strengthens local communities. The concept has, however, attracted controversy: some residents have interpreted associated traffic measures as restrictions on their freedom of movement, prompting debate about how such schemes are communicated and implemented.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:46246b77390b','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Why has the concept attracted controversy?',array['It is too expensive.','It increases car use.','It closes schools.','Some residents saw traffic measures as limits on their freedom.']::text[],'D','''...some residents have interpreted associated traffic measures as restrictions on their freedom of movement.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','''Fifteen-minute cities'' are urban areas designed so that residents can reach most daily needs — shops, schools, health services and parks — within a fifteen-minute walk or cycle. Proponents argue the model reduces car dependence, improves health and strengthens local communities. The concept has, however, attracted controversy: some residents have interpreted associated traffic measures as restrictions on their freedom of movement, prompting debate about how such schemes are communicated and implemented.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:5ed9af0e3635','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Which benefit do proponents NOT mention?',array['higher property prices','better health','stronger communities','less car dependence']::text[],'A','Proponents mention reduced car dependence, health and community.',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','''Fifteen-minute cities'' are urban areas designed so that residents can reach most daily needs — shops, schools, health services and parks — within a fifteen-minute walk or cycle. Proponents argue the model reduces car dependence, improves health and strengthens local communities. The concept has, however, attracted controversy: some residents have interpreted associated traffic measures as restrictions on their freedom of movement, prompting debate about how such schemes are communicated and implemented.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:16ea315ac6b3','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Why do scientists stress less visible organisms?',array['They support processes agriculture depends on.','They are more beautiful.','They are easier to study.','They receive most funding.']::text[],'A','''These organisms underpin processes such as decomposition, pollination and nutrient cycling on which agriculture depends.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Biodiversity loss is often discussed in terms of charismatic species such as tigers and whales, but scientists stress that the decline of less visible organisms — insects, fungi and soil microbes — may have equally serious consequences. These organisms underpin processes such as decomposition, pollination and nutrient cycling on which agriculture depends. Because they are less studied, however, the scale of their decline is harder to measure, and conservation funding tends to favour species that capture public attention.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:6274710c85c8','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Why is the decline of insects and fungi harder to measure?',array['They are too small to see.','They live only in the ocean.','They are less studied.','They change colour.']::text[],'C','''Because they are less studied, however, the scale of their decline is harder to measure.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Biodiversity loss is often discussed in terms of charismatic species such as tigers and whales, but scientists stress that the decline of less visible organisms — insects, fungi and soil microbes — may have equally serious consequences. These organisms underpin processes such as decomposition, pollination and nutrient cycling on which agriculture depends. Because they are less studied, however, the scale of their decline is harder to measure, and conservation funding tends to favour species that capture public attention.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:81b5907025e0','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What bias in conservation funding is mentioned?',array['It favours insects.','It favours species that capture public attention.','It is equally distributed.','It ignores large animals.']::text[],'B','''...conservation funding tends to favour species that capture public attention.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Biodiversity loss is often discussed in terms of charismatic species such as tigers and whales, but scientists stress that the decline of less visible organisms — insects, fungi and soil microbes — may have equally serious consequences. These organisms underpin processes such as decomposition, pollination and nutrient cycling on which agriculture depends. Because they are less studied, however, the scale of their decline is harder to measure, and conservation funding tends to favour species that capture public attention.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:281430ecfd17','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What does recent research suggest about video games?',array['Only puzzle games are harmful.','Games have no effects at all.','Some games may improve certain skills.','All games cause aggression.']::text[],'C','''...a growing body of research presents a more nuanced picture.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Video games have long been criticised as a waste of time or a cause of aggression, but a growing body of research presents a more nuanced picture. Certain action games appear to improve visual attention and reaction times, while puzzle and strategy games may enhance problem-solving skills. Researchers caution, however, that the benefits depend heavily on the type of game and the amount of time spent playing, and that excessive gaming can displace sleep and physical activity.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:b6d5e187ea12','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Which skill may action games improve?',array['visual attention and reaction times','vocabulary','spelling','long-term memory']::text[],'A','''Certain action games appear to improve visual attention and reaction times.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Video games have long been criticised as a waste of time or a cause of aggression, but a growing body of research presents a more nuanced picture. Certain action games appear to improve visual attention and reaction times, while puzzle and strategy games may enhance problem-solving skills. Researchers caution, however, that the benefits depend heavily on the type of game and the amount of time spent playing, and that excessive gaming can displace sleep and physical activity.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:68da841cbd39','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What caution do researchers give?',array['All games are equally beneficial.','Games should be banned for adults.','Only strategy games are safe.','Benefits depend on game type and playing time.']::text[],'D','''...the benefits depend heavily on the type of game and the amount of time spent playing.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Video games have long been criticised as a waste of time or a cause of aggression, but a growing body of research presents a more nuanced picture. Certain action games appear to improve visual attention and reaction times, while puzzle and strategy games may enhance problem-solving skills. Researchers caution, however, that the benefits depend heavily on the type of game and the amount of time spent playing, and that excessive gaming can displace sleep and physical activity.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:237b523e3741','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Where does recycling rank in the waste hierarchy?',array['at the top','below reduction and reuse','above reuse','at the same level as landfill']::text[],'B','''...it ranks below reduction and reuse in the so-called waste hierarchy.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Recycling is often presented as the cornerstone of environmental responsibility, yet waste experts emphasise that it ranks below reduction and reuse in the so-called waste hierarchy. Recycling still requires energy and transport, and some materials, notably many plastics, can be recycled only a limited number of times before their quality degrades. Moreover, contaminated recycling — items that are dirty or wrongly sorted — can result in entire loads being sent to landfill.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:38727abf09e2','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What limitation of plastic recycling is mentioned?',array['It requires no energy.','It is never recycled.','It can only be recycled a limited number of times.','It improves with each cycle.']::text[],'C','''...can be recycled only a limited number of times before their quality degrades.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Recycling is often presented as the cornerstone of environmental responsibility, yet waste experts emphasise that it ranks below reduction and reuse in the so-called waste hierarchy. Recycling still requires energy and transport, and some materials, notably many plastics, can be recycled only a limited number of times before their quality degrades. Moreover, contaminated recycling — items that are dirty or wrongly sorted — can result in entire loads being sent to landfill.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:ce3192a77e3e','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What can happen to contaminated recycling?',array['It is exported.','It is turned into fuel.','Whole loads may be sent to landfill.','It is cleaned for free.']::text[],'C','''...can result in entire loads being sent to landfill.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Recycling is often presented as the cornerstone of environmental responsibility, yet waste experts emphasise that it ranks below reduction and reuse in the so-called waste hierarchy. Recycling still requires energy and transport, and some materials, notably many plastics, can be recycled only a limited number of times before their quality degrades. Moreover, contaminated recycling — items that are dirty or wrongly sorted — can result in entire loads being sent to landfill.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:8e25532a5fd1','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What benefit do mentors report?',array['faster promotion','higher salaries','fewer responsibilities','fresh perspectives and better understanding of junior staff']::text[],'D','''...mentors themselves... report gaining fresh perspectives.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Formal mentoring schemes pair less experienced employees with senior colleagues who offer guidance on career development. Evaluations suggest that mentees often benefit from greater confidence and faster promotion. Less widely recognised is the benefit to mentors themselves, who report gaining fresh perspectives and a deeper understanding of junior staff''s challenges. Schemes appear most effective when participants have a say in who they are paired with, rather than being assigned arbitrarily.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:a7f0ec6ea013','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','When are mentoring schemes most effective?',array['when mentors are paid extra','when participants have a say in their pairing','when sessions are daily','when pairs are assigned randomly']::text[],'B','''...most effective when participants have a say in who they are paired with.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Formal mentoring schemes pair less experienced employees with senior colleagues who offer guidance on career development. Evaluations suggest that mentees often benefit from greater confidence and faster promotion. Less widely recognised is the benefit to mentors themselves, who report gaining fresh perspectives and a deeper understanding of junior staff''s challenges. Schemes appear most effective when participants have a say in who they are paired with, rather than being assigned arbitrarily.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:c4deea056aaf','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What benefit do mentees often gain?',array['a pay rise immediately','fewer working hours','a new manager','greater confidence and faster promotion']::text[],'D','''...mentees often benefit from greater confidence and faster promotion.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Formal mentoring schemes pair less experienced employees with senior colleagues who offer guidance on career development. Evaluations suggest that mentees often benefit from greater confidence and faster promotion. Less widely recognised is the benefit to mentors themselves, who report gaining fresh perspectives and a deeper understanding of junior staff''s challenges. Schemes appear most effective when participants have a say in who they are paired with, rather than being assigned arbitrarily.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:a94cb1dbbed1','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What does machine translation still struggle with?',array['simple sentences','common words','everyday messages','ambiguity, humour and cultural references']::text[],'D','''...it still struggles with ambiguity, humour, cultural references and specialised terminology.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Machine translation has improved dramatically, and for many everyday purposes it is now remarkably accurate. Professional translators, however, point out that it still struggles with ambiguity, humour, cultural references and specialised terminology. In legal and medical contexts, where errors can have serious consequences, human review remains essential. Many translators now work as ''post-editors'', correcting and refining machine output rather than translating from scratch.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:7ffb415f8d2d','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','In which contexts is human review essential?',array['personal emails','social media','tourism','legal and medical']::text[],'D','''In legal and medical contexts... human review remains essential.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Machine translation has improved dramatically, and for many everyday purposes it is now remarkably accurate. Professional translators, however, point out that it still struggles with ambiguity, humour, cultural references and specialised terminology. In legal and medical contexts, where errors can have serious consequences, human review remains essential. Many translators now work as ''post-editors'', correcting and refining machine output rather than translating from scratch.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:4570d7178ebe','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What is a ''post-editor''?',array['a software engineer','a newspaper editor','someone who posts letters','a translator who corrects machine output']::text[],'D','''...correcting and refining machine output rather than translating from scratch.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Machine translation has improved dramatically, and for many everyday purposes it is now remarkably accurate. Professional translators, however, point out that it still struggles with ambiguity, humour, cultural references and specialised terminology. In legal and medical contexts, where errors can have serious consequences, human review remains essential. Many translators now work as ''post-editors'', correcting and refining machine output rather than translating from scratch.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:2f844c532f55','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What dilemma do conservators face?',array['how to raise money','whether to demolish the building','whether to restore the original look or keep later changes','whether to open it to the public']::text[],'C','''...should they return it to its original appearance, or preserve the alterations...''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','When a historic building is restored, conservators face a difficult choice: should they return it to its original appearance, or preserve the alterations made over the centuries, which are themselves part of its history? Many modern conservation guidelines favour minimal intervention, repairing rather than replacing, and ensuring that new work is distinguishable from old. Critics argue that this approach can leave buildings looking unfinished, whereas supporters see it as more honest.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:7e7f439ddcbb','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What do modern guidelines favour?',array['copying the original exactly','removing all later additions','minimal intervention and distinguishable new work','complete rebuilding']::text[],'C','''...favour minimal intervention... ensuring that new work is distinguishable from old.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','When a historic building is restored, conservators face a difficult choice: should they return it to its original appearance, or preserve the alterations made over the centuries, which are themselves part of its history? Many modern conservation guidelines favour minimal intervention, repairing rather than replacing, and ensuring that new work is distinguishable from old. Critics argue that this approach can leave buildings looking unfinished, whereas supporters see it as more honest.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:19c35072df15','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','How do supporters view the minimal approach?',array['as more beautiful','as faster','as more honest','as cheaper']::text[],'C','''...supporters see it as more honest.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','When a historic building is restored, conservators face a difficult choice: should they return it to its original appearance, or preserve the alterations made over the centuries, which are themselves part of its history? Many modern conservation guidelines favour minimal intervention, repairing rather than replacing, and ensuring that new work is distinguishable from old. Critics argue that this approach can leave buildings looking unfinished, whereas supporters see it as more honest.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:3e0d785343c3','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','How is tipping viewed in Japan?',array['a legal requirement','compulsory','uncommon and sometimes embarrassing','rude not to tip']::text[],'C','''In Japan... tipping is uncommon and can even cause embarrassment.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Tipping customs vary enormously between countries. In the United States, tips form a substantial part of many service workers'' income, and failing to tip is widely regarded as rude. In Japan, by contrast, tipping is uncommon and can even cause embarrassment. In the UK, a discretionary service charge of around 12.5% is often added to restaurant bills, and recent legislation requires that tips be passed on to staff in full.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:0c0c1cff6d21','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What does recent UK legislation require?',array['a 20% service charge','that tipping be banned','that customers tip in cash','that tips go to staff in full']::text[],'D','''...recent legislation requires that tips be passed on to staff in full.''',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Tipping customs vary enormously between countries. In the United States, tips form a substantial part of many service workers'' income, and failing to tip is widely regarded as rude. In Japan, by contrast, tipping is uncommon and can even cause embarrassment. In the UK, a discretionary service charge of around 12.5% is often added to restaurant bills, and recent legislation requires that tips be passed on to staff in full.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:7d7e212b1e1e','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What does ''discretionary'' service charge mean?',array['it is included in the price','it is required by law','it goes to the government','the customer may choose not to pay it']::text[],'D','Discretionary = left to the customer''s choice.',array['reading','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09','Tipping customs vary enormously between countries. In the United States, tips form a substantial part of many service workers'' income, and failing to tip is widely regarded as rude. In Japan, by contrast, tipping is uncommon and can even cause embarrassment. In the UK, a discretionary service charge of around 12.5% is often added to restaurant bills, and recent legislation requires that tips be passed on to staff in full.',null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:68eec6736a27','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','Scarcely had the meeting begun ___ the fire alarm went off.',array['then','when','that','than']::text[],'B','''Scarcely had... when''.',array['grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:6ff7fe865d72','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','Not once ___ she complain about the conditions.',array['was','did','does','had']::text[],'B','''Not once'' + inversion with ''did''.',array['grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:5b783b8e989f','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','Never before ___ such a large crowd gathered in the square.',array['had','was','has','did']::text[],'A','''Never before had...'' (past perfect inversion).',array['grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:c0f9f1c89d18','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','The evidence, ___ it is, points to an inside job.',array['such as','as such','so as','such that']::text[],'A','''Such as it is'' = although limited.',array['grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:179fd1699471','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','She left the room without ___ a word.',array['to say','say','said','saying']::text[],'D','''Without + -ing''.',array['grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:b4e2672e5316','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','It''s no ___ that she won — she trained harder than anyone.',array['miracle','surprise of','wonder','doubt up']::text[],'C','''It''s no wonder'' = not surprising.',array['grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:5a54305d6c76','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','There is every ___ that the deal will go ahead.',array['likeliness up','likeness','likely','likelihood']::text[],'D','''Every likelihood'' = high probability.',array['grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:28c24b4a4ed0','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','I''d rather ___ nothing than lie.',array['saying','say','to say','said']::text[],'B','''Would rather'' + base form.',array['grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:41370a2a2ee6','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','He is by no ___ the only person to blame.',array['means','account','way','chance']::text[],'A','''By no means'' = not at all.',array['grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:ccb38f6e4f6b','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','On ___ of the board, I''d like to thank you.',array['side','half','part','behalf']::text[],'D','''On behalf of'' = representing.',array['grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:3fcc182f99ab','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','It remains ___ seen whether the policy will work.',array['be','being','to be','to']::text[],'C','''It remains to be seen''.',array['grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:3adcdb5fc412','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','The project, ___ costs had been underestimated, ran into trouble.',array['its','which','of which its','whose']::text[],'D','''Whose'' for possession by a thing.',array['grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:632cae4b5894','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','I''ll lend you the car on the ___ that you fill it up.',array['conditional','condition','conditions','conditioning']::text[],'B','''On the condition that''.',array['grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:a2588f8cce45','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','She spoke as though she ___ the whole story.',array['knows','has known','knew','will know']::text[],'C','''As though'' + past simple for a present unreal situation.',array['grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:d779aa1bc800','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','___ we to cancel now, we would lose the deposit.',array['Should','If','Were','Had']::text[],'C','''Were we to'' = if we were to.',array['grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:a42ad053e6dd','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','The longer you leave it, the ___ it will be to fix.',array['harder','hard','hardest','more hard']::text[],'A','Double comparative.',array['grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:78e97a599f56','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','He denies ___ any knowledge of the affair.',array['to have had','had','having had','have had']::text[],'C','''Deny'' + perfect -ing.',array['grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:197fc09e474e','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','The museum is closed ___ further notice.',array['to','since','until','by']::text[],'C','''Until further notice''.',array['grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:bf59274c1f4d','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','___ of the evidence, the jury reached a verdict.',array['In the light up','In light','By light','On light']::text[],'B','''In light of'' = considering.',array['grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:8efcadf82e80','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','The report was released ___ public pressure.',array['responding at','in response to','as response of','in response for']::text[],'B','''In response to''.',array['grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:819140106b42','C1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The company''s profits have ___ in recent years.',array['plumped','plumbed','plundered','plummeted']::text[],'D','To plummet = fall rapidly.',array['vocabulary']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:9134e2012efb','C1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The government has been ___ for its slow response.',array['lamented','lambasted','lampooned up','laminated']::text[],'B','Lambasted = criticised harshly.',array['vocabulary']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:c0e9301bfa89','C1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','There''s a ___ of truth in what he says.',array['grind','grin','grain','gram']::text[],'C','''A grain of truth'' = a small amount.',array['vocabulary']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:741f63095825','C1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The new policy is a ___ departure from the past.',array['radiant','radial','radically','radical']::text[],'D','A radical departure = a big change.',array['vocabulary']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:4ff52bc77b64','C1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','She has a ___ grasp of the facts.',array['solid up','firmly','firm','fixed up']::text[],'C','''A firm grasp'' = a good understanding.',array['vocabulary']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:0d7d8d0885f9','C1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The film is ___ entertaining.',array['throughout','thorough','thoroughly','through']::text[],'C','Thoroughly = completely.',array['vocabulary']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:76675040f333','C1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','He was ___ dismissed from his post.',array['summarily','summarised','summery','summary']::text[],'A','Summarily = immediately, without formality.',array['vocabulary']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:605abdbf7d54','C1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The building''s design has been ___ as a masterpiece.',array['haled','hauled','hailing up','hailed']::text[],'D','Hailed = praised enthusiastically.',array['vocabulary']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-09:fbb9a66bc177','C1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The meeting ended in ___ — no decision was reached.',array['lockdown','dead end up','deadline','deadlock']::text[],'D','Deadlock = a situation where no progress is possible.',array['vocabulary']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-09',null,null,null,null,'practice'),
